{"ts": 0.03572, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mMODULE — shells: what runs your commands\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree short lessons, then a gate. This module stands alone and saves\r\nnothing. Type \u001b[92mquit\u001b[0m to leave at any point.\r\n\r\nYou will look at three things:\r\n  the shell is a program you can inspect\r\n  other shells exist, and what they change\r\n  your login shell and this tutor's shell can differ\r\n\r\nEverything is read-only except one small file at the gate, written\r\ninside \u001b[94m/var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-pvwqz5_5/shells\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to begin lesson 1.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 581}
{"ts": 0.035839, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
