{"ts": 0.088697, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells 2 — other shells exist\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nFour shells you will meet:\r\n  \u001b[92mbash\u001b[0m   common on Linux; the shell this tutor runs\r\n  \u001b[92mzsh\u001b[0m    the default on current macOS\r\n  \u001b[92mfish\u001b[0m   a shell with its own syntax, installed separately\r\n", "len": 253}
{"ts": 0.088766, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[92msh\u001b[0m     the minimal standard shell, used by scripts\r\n\r\nAsk which of two are installed here:\r\n  \u001b[92mcommand -v zsh fish\u001b[0m   \u001b[90m# one path per shell found\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[36mDifferent\u001b[0m: configuration syntax, prompt, completion.\r\n\u001b[36mThe same\u001b[0m: the programs (\u001b[92mls\u001b[0m, \u001b[92mcat\u001b[0m), paths, pipes, redirection.\r\nNotice that no output means that shell is not installed. That is normal.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Run the check, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 460}
{"ts": 0.092004, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
