{"ts": 0.208982, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells — task\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nFind out whether \u001b[92mzsh\u001b[0m is installed here, and record the answer in a\r\nfile. You will work inside \u001b[94m/var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-pvwqz5_5/shells\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n  1. ask the shell where \u001b[92mzsh\u001b[0m is\r\n  2. send what it prints to a file named \u001b[94mzsh.txt\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 333}
{"ts": 0.209037, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "     \u001b[90m(hint: Stage 4's \u001b[92m>\u001b[0m\u001b[90m sends output to a file)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nIf zsh is not installed, the shell prints nothing, and the file is\r\nempty. That is a correct answer.\r\n\r\n\u001b[90mI will check: zsh.txt exists and holds exactly what \u001b[0m\u001b[92mcommand -v zsh\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mprints on this machine, and your history shows you asked.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[93m when done.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 382}
{"ts": 0.211762, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mcheck\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(test your work)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(the task again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 132}
